  "interpretation": [
    "All 12 aggregate funding-augmented models (3 lags x 4 labels) have worse MSE than fixed price/volume controls. This rejects useful predictive increment for this model specification, not all potential funding mechanisms.",
    "The f20 positive-vs-negative unconditional spread is confounded with time regimes: all 84 decisions in fixed period 184:268 are positive and share growth exceeds prior training ranges. Block bootstrap does not by itself resolve this regime confounding.",
    "Entry-day funding filter catches 40.576% negative amount and misses 21.902% positive amount at lag1, versus baseline 47.979% and 32.624%. This is a tradeoff with fewer rejected events, not a simultaneous improvement in both rates.",
    "persist5 equals positive-day count divided by 5 minus 0.5: exact zero group is mathematically impossible, not a data gap."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Fund publication and revision PIT not authenticated; next-session availability is a stated assumption.",
    "MSE and loss-filter results are event-level diagnostics on seen development data, not account qualification.",
    "Four primary price/share quadrants plus zero/flat partitions are descriptive and cannot establish causality or eliminate arbitrage/product-substitution alternatives.",
    "Does not rerun exchange execution simulation or verify provider historical revisions."
  ]
